# How the main screen takes a change of size. `resize` moves the window's side a step at a
# time, as a hand dragging it does, and `drag` does the same with a pane's divider. Each says
# which faults the change brings and from what size, which texts jump, and whether part of
# the screen follows a frame late. One axis at a time, so a text that moves along the other
# one is a reflow.
settle 300

resize narrower 640 900
size 1600 900
resize shorter 1600 420
size 1600 900
settle 60

# Each pane from its narrowest to its widest. With both at their widest the block map between
# them has the least room it can have.
drag left_pane_narrower "Left Pane Divider" -300 0
drag left_pane_wider "Left Pane Divider" 600 0
drag right_pane_wider "Right Pane Divider" -330 0
drag right_pane_narrower "Right Pane Divider" 600 0
